{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"pointer-events-none select-none whitespace-nowrap text-center text-[min(800px,41.9vw)] font-extrabold leading-[0.645] tracking-[-0.0575em] text-[#9b9b9b] opacity-[0.07]","children":"poulo"}]]}]]}]}]
3d:["$","p","The users were General Contractors, their workers, and subcontractors operating on construction sites, not desk workers, so I had to design for real world constraints: small screens, one handed use, noisy environments, and workflows that needed to be completed quickly and without confusion. Every screen had to earn its place. I focused heavily on task clarity, reducing cognitive load, and making the most common actions immediately accessible without deep navigation.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"The users were General Contractors, their workers, and subcontractors operating on construction sites, not desk workers, so I had to design for real world constraints: small screens, one handed use, noisy environments, and workflows that needed to be completed quickly and without confusion. Every screen had to earn its place. I focused heavily on task clarity, reducing cognitive load, and making the most common actions immediately accessible without deep navigation."}]
3e:["$","p","The triage and discovery phase was critical here. I spent time understanding how GCs and their teams actually move through their day on site, what information they need at a glance versus what can be secondary, and where the existing process created friction. That shaped the information architecture and interaction model from the ground up.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"The triage and discovery phase was critical here. I spent time understanding how GCs and their teams actually move through their day on site, what information they need at a glance versus what can be secondary, and where the existing process created friction. That shaped the information architecture and interaction model from the ground up."}]
